00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:57,730
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:01:57,970 --> 00:02:02,160
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION.

3
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:40,110
Let's get started, son.

4
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:43,720
Come on.
"In the name of God, the infinitely
Compassionate and Merciful." (Basmala).

5
00:02:44,610 --> 00:02:46,040
Eternal Allah!

6
00:02:47,850 --> 00:02:50,130
- Allah is Great!
- Allah is one!

7
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:52,590
- Allah is Great!
- Allah is one!

8
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:55,430
- Allah is Great!
- Allah is one!

9
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:58,720
- Allah is Great!
- Allah is one!

10
00:02:59,010 --> 00:03:01,600
My Osman, give it a break.

11
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:05,830
Everything has its time.

12
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:08,620
Everything has its time, son.

13
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:21,880
This is my wedding gift for my Aybars,
Bamsı Bey.

14
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,720
This weapon needs to be done before
the next night comes.

15
00:03:26,630 --> 00:03:28,880
I kept my every word that I gave to him.

16
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:31,380
Look at them, hey!

17
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:35,890
Both my Osman and my Aybars grew up...

18
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:38,570
and they became blood brothers.

19
00:03:38,910 --> 00:03:43,600
With my father Ertuğrul Ghazi, we follow
your friendship, my Bamsı Bey.

20
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:45,450
Thank my Allah.

21
00:03:45,470 --> 00:03:48,080
Thank my Allah, I've seen these days.

22
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:50,670
Praise be my valiant!
Praise be! (Masha Allah)

23
00:03:51,290 --> 00:03:54,010
So, my Osman, what do you think?

24
00:03:54,410 --> 00:03:57,230
Will our Ertuğrul Ghazi return from Konya?

25
00:03:57,990 --> 00:04:01,700
Will Sultan and Dahi Beys
accept his offer?

26
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:04,800
We realized our homeland's fire together
with...

27
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:07,170
my ancestor Alparslan in
Malazgirt, Bamsı Bey.

28
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,880
We were rookie, we are masters now.

29
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:15,430
We tolerated everything.

30
00:04:16,370 --> 00:04:18,690
We fought fearlessly to...

31
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:20,520
call this land our homeland.

32
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:27,810
Now, it is time to turn these small
shrubs into a luscious tree.

33
00:04:28,730 --> 00:04:33,620
Under the luscious tree, brave men
and magnificent women...

34
00:04:33,630 --> 00:04:36,050
will pave the way for a new state.

35
00:04:37,260 --> 00:04:41,100
All the enemies, all the traitors...

36
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:43,820
We will destroy them with this fire.

37
00:04:46,570 --> 00:04:49,240
No matter what results come from Konya...

38
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:53,530
We won't let my father's flag fall.

39
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:56,390
May Allah be my witness...

40
00:04:57,110 --> 00:05:00,360
my children and I will fight resolutely
to...

41
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:04,840
spread this blessed flag to
all the world.

42
00:05:05,470 --> 00:05:06,820
Masha Allah (praise be).

43
00:05:06,930 --> 00:05:08,750
Masha Allah my valiant.

44
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:13,360
Now that I heard these from you,
I will die in peace.

45
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:16,810
Our Ertuğrul Bey's objective is in
progress.

46
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:19,250
Our Ertuğrul Bey's objective is in
progress.

47
00:05:47,620 --> 00:05:50,960
My father Süleyman Shah had this boil too.

48
00:05:52,790 --> 00:05:55,870
Look at the difficulty this malady is
giving to me, Hatun...

49
00:05:55,870 --> 00:05:59,890
while I have Ertuğrul Bey's trust in my
Shoulders.

50
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:07,000
Little things don't hurt the great.

51
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:09,220
You are Dündar Bey.

52
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:12,950
You will get over every difficulty
for sure.

53
00:06:17,950 --> 00:06:22,480
Everybody looks, but my brother Ertuğrul
Bey sees.

54
00:06:23,870 --> 00:06:27,800
We are harvesting what he seeded...

55
00:06:28,570 --> 00:06:30,780
twenty-five years ago.

56
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:37,130
This agreement will bring
peace and welfare, Hatun.

57
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:48,380
Don't underestimate yourself, Dündar Bey.

58
00:06:49,210 --> 00:06:53,090
You need to walk with friends, not strangers.

59
00:07:01,370 --> 00:07:06,140
What would happen if you stepped back
like Gündoğdu and Sungurtekin?

60
00:07:08,510 --> 00:07:12,880
Ertuğrul Bey gained power thanks to
your support.

61
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:22,540
Everyone has some power.

62
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:27,580
But only you have power and skills.

63
00:07:39,650 --> 00:07:40,950
Also...

64
00:07:41,610 --> 00:07:43,410
you talk about peace, but...

65
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:48,810
snakes, who fear from peace, are already
out there.

66
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:52,140
You need to be careful.

67
00:07:52,750 --> 00:07:54,860
May my Allah be my witness...

68
00:07:55,600 --> 00:08:00,870
I'll burn those snakes alive.

69
00:08:01,650 --> 00:08:03,060
I will.

70
00:08:06,670 --> 00:08:10,670
I gave my word to my brother Ertuğrul Bey.

71
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:13,340
I will carry this out.

72
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,320
Let's go.

73
00:08:16,530 --> 00:08:19,090
Let's not keep Governor Yorgepolos wait.

74
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:26,210
I wish to be blessed by you before
taking off.

75
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:28,590
Oy, oy son.

76
00:08:29,690 --> 00:08:33,330
Your father's prayers are always with you, son.

77
00:08:34,140 --> 00:08:39,090
However, we can't trust them.

78
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:42,640
Be careful, son.
Okay?

79
00:08:42,770 --> 00:08:48,850
Don't worry, father. I am the son of
retired Head Alp Bamsı.

80
00:08:48,950 --> 00:08:51,940
The enemy who faces me knows that I am
the winner.

81
00:08:54,650 --> 00:08:57,170
Thank you, son.
Thank you (Eyvallah)

82
00:08:58,030 --> 00:08:59,400
However...

83
00:08:59,870 --> 00:09:01,960
you should know that...

84
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:06,540
braveness cannot always deal with treason.

85
00:09:08,010 --> 00:09:10,240
You need to be careful.

86
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:14,670
You need to foresee the enemy behind you.

87
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:17,230
Who can foresee the enemy, father?

88
00:09:17,310 --> 00:09:18,910
Bey does, son.

89
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:21,570
Bey(Master) knows.

90
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:24,530
Look, this is my Oğuz Ancestor's advice.

91
00:09:24,550 --> 00:09:27,660
Whatever happens to Oğuz happens whilst
he sleeps.

92
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:30,510
The valiant who doesn't sleep can foresee,
son.

93
00:09:30,730 --> 00:09:33,260
Some people are walking asleep.

94
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:37,910
However, Bey, who is awake even if when
he sleeps...

95
00:09:38,030 --> 00:09:40,660
can foresee the enemy, son.

96
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:44,150
I think you missed Ertuğrul Ghazi, father.

97
00:09:46,580 --> 00:09:48,780
Oy, my Ertuğrul Bey.

98
00:09:49,670 --> 00:09:52,600
No, son.
You miss who you can't see.

99
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:54,570
You have miss who you can't see.

100
00:09:54,570 --> 00:09:55,810
Son...

101
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:59,560
I see Ertuğrul Bey in Osman.

102
00:09:59,650 --> 00:10:05,200
His looks, his behaviors, his stand...
He carries them all.

103
00:10:08,140 --> 00:10:12,690
You cannot see a valiant like him
every day.

104
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:17,690
Son, my wish is that you shall be
among the ones who are with him.

105
00:10:26,910 --> 00:10:33,470
Look, son. This is not a will from father.
This is a will from your ancestor.

106
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:39,260
Stand with Osman...

107
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:43,850
just like I stood with Ertuğrul Bey.

108
00:10:47,530 --> 00:10:48,990
Ayşe Hatun.

109
00:10:49,050 --> 00:10:53,750
Shall we take our traditional
carpets to them also?

110
00:10:54,260 --> 00:10:56,750
I knew you would want them too,
my Gündüz Bey(master)

111
00:10:56,910 --> 00:10:59,750
- I prepared them last night.
- Thank you (Eyvallah) Hatun.

112
00:11:00,030 --> 00:11:01,200
Thank you. (Eyvallah)

113
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:04,460
It is obvious that you are from here.

114
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:07,560
Let's go.

115
00:11:21,870 --> 00:11:23,550
Hay Masha Allah (praise be!)

116
00:11:24,110 --> 00:11:25,640
Masha Allah.

117
00:11:35,970 --> 00:11:37,910
- Burçin.
- Aybras.

118
00:11:38,210 --> 00:11:39,960
Do you have to go?

119
00:11:40,750 --> 00:11:43,650
We have henna night tonight.

120
00:11:43,930 --> 00:11:45,520
Stay in the tent.

121
00:11:46,380 --> 00:11:50,280
You know,
mission is the priority for the Alps.

122
00:11:50,530 --> 00:11:53,430
Also, I can't leave Osman Bey
alone, Burçin.

123
00:11:53,710 --> 00:11:57,310
Pray for us so that we can go fast and
come back well.

124
00:11:58,940 --> 00:12:00,530
In sha Allah (if Allah permits).

125
00:12:00,590 --> 00:12:03,000
May Allah open your road, Aybars.

126
00:12:08,390 --> 00:12:10,150
Just a little time left.

127
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:14,470
Tonight, these hands will
be applied henna of our wedding.

128
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:23,760
Aygul prepared henna for me.

129
00:12:23,780 --> 00:12:25,490
It was so beautiful.

130
00:12:26,430 --> 00:12:29,530
If only you could see yourself
in the view of my eyes.

131
00:12:29,870 --> 00:12:31,710
You are so beautiful.

132
00:12:34,810 --> 00:12:36,100
Go.

133
00:12:36,290 --> 00:12:37,900
They are waiting for you.

134
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:52,710
My Burçin, you are entrusted to Allah.

135
00:12:52,970 --> 00:12:54,590
You too, my Aybars.

136
00:12:54,790 --> 00:12:56,060
You too.

137
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:55,950
Ey Kayı's Alps(men)

138
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:59,340
You are ready to fire.

139
00:14:00,130 --> 00:14:05,200
Your body shows nobility, and your
heart shows the fire inside you.

140
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:11,100
- Masha Allah, Masha Allah! (praise be!)
- Thank you (Eyvallah) my Bey!

141
00:14:28,550 --> 00:14:30,080
What are these, son?

142
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:36,700
These are the weapons we will
present to the governor, father.

143
00:14:38,310 --> 00:14:43,890
Osman, you are the master of weapons here.

144
00:14:44,990 --> 00:14:51,280
Check them, see if our friend Governor
Yorgepolos would like these.

145
00:15:08,150 --> 00:15:11,590
We will give these as a gift.
And, we are going to attack...

146
00:15:11,610 --> 00:15:13,670
his castle with these weapons.

147
00:15:16,830 --> 00:15:18,910
Why wouldn't he like it, Dündar Bey?

148
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:29,700
Dündar Bey.

149
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:31,530
Dündar Bey.

150
00:15:33,070 --> 00:15:35,940
Other than Kayıs are strangers.

151
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,820
Just in case...

152
00:15:37,820 --> 00:15:39,880
shall I come with you?

153
00:15:39,930 --> 00:15:41,280
What do you say?

154
00:15:45,390 --> 00:15:48,760
We need a hand in our tent, Bamsı Bey.

155
00:15:49,230 --> 00:15:54,260
You stay here, finish the preparations,
and take care of the tent.

156
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:56,770
Okay(Eyvallah) Dündar Bey.

157
00:16:01,470 --> 00:16:04,470
Let us depart.

158
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:35,720
Come on.

159
00:16:50,930 --> 00:16:54,690
You are entrusted to Allah.
Go fast and come back well.

160
00:17:14,210 --> 00:17:19,400
Tekfur Yorgopolos, both the peace and
trade agreements are like what we want.

161
00:17:19,470 --> 00:17:23,980
However, the indemnity for caravan raids
cannot be accepted.

162
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:26,290
Don't worry, Kalanos.

163
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:30,150
- No power can make me sign it.
- I don't have any doubt.

164
00:17:31,330 --> 00:17:36,320
We paved the way for this agreement with
Ertuğrul, but...

165
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:40,840
his brother Dündar wants to be the man
to finish it.

166
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:44,590
Of course he wants.
He wants to show his power to everyone.

167
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:52,120
With god's will,
we will be superior all the time

168
00:17:54,190 --> 00:17:59,730
This is a talisman which is to protect
my husband.

169
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:20,780
As long as you are with me, nothing can
hurt me.

170
00:18:21,710 --> 00:18:23,850
I am a very lucky man.

171
00:18:27,270 --> 00:18:29,770
We should be careful anyways.

172
00:18:30,650 --> 00:18:34,100
The stars on the sky last night
annoyed me.

173
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:38,450
You may consider this a superstition, but
they annoyed me.

174
00:18:38,450 --> 00:18:40,280
Don't worry about me, Sofya.

175
00:18:40,470 --> 00:18:44,080
Commander Kalanos, the greatest warrior of
Bithynia...

176
00:18:45,950 --> 00:18:47,810
is to protect me.

177
00:18:53,540 --> 00:18:55,140
Kayıs are coming, sir.

178
00:19:02,420 --> 00:19:04,200
Respected Governor!

179
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:47,610
Welcome (in distance)

180
00:19:48,370 --> 00:19:49,870
Welcome (in distance)

181
00:20:19,550 --> 00:20:23,360
- Welcome, Dündar Bey.
- Thank you Governor Yorgopolos.

182
00:20:23,750 --> 00:20:25,180
Princess Sofia.

183
00:20:26,390 --> 00:20:29,540
Welcome, Kayı's women.

184
00:20:31,280 --> 00:20:33,390
You honored our castle.

185
00:20:33,390 --> 00:20:35,500
We are honored too, princess.

186
00:20:37,450 --> 00:20:40,790
I wish Ertuğrul Bey had been with us
on this beautiful day.

187
00:20:41,260 --> 00:20:44,440
We owe this happiness to him.

188
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:50,620
The show is starting.

189
00:20:52,170 --> 00:20:53,460
Ertuğrul!

190
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:58,210
If what you want is me, Governor,
here I am!

191
00:20:58,380 --> 00:21:02,380
Neither I nor you fear from each other...

192
00:21:02,610 --> 00:21:05,030
until this day.

193
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:07,090
Let's finish this!

194
00:21:13,820 --> 00:21:16,190
Enough!
This war should end.

195
00:21:16,210 --> 00:21:19,730
I want to build trust between us.

196
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:24,420
Shall my people have a full belly and
a happy heart.

197
00:21:24,450 --> 00:21:28,190
Long live!
Long live!

198
00:21:28,430 --> 00:21:32,080
Long live!
Long live!

199
00:21:32,910 --> 00:21:36,550
We decided to fight till the last
drop of our blood.

200
00:21:36,590 --> 00:21:39,590
Now we decided to make peace.

201
00:21:39,700 --> 00:21:43,070
Long live!
Long live!

202
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:46,920
Then, with my brother Dündar...

203
00:21:47,010 --> 00:21:48,800
we shall make peace with you.

204
00:21:48,830 --> 00:21:51,030
I'll go to Konya.

205
00:21:51,140 --> 00:21:55,080
When I come back, we will celebrate
this agreement.

206
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:59,650
Governor Yorgopolos, you are an honorable
man.

207
00:21:59,660 --> 00:22:02,120
You are wise as well as a good soldier.

208
00:22:02,190 --> 00:22:04,250
As to Ertuğrul Bey...

209
00:22:04,580 --> 00:22:06,630
As to Ertuğrul Bey...

210
00:22:07,870 --> 00:22:10,840
All the Bithynia knows how brave he is.

211
00:22:12,510 --> 00:22:16,440
He feeds the poors.
He clothes the naked.

212
00:22:17,730 --> 00:22:19,980
He saves the debtor.

213
00:22:20,180 --> 00:22:24,730
He doesn't distinguish müslims and
non-müslims.

214
00:22:29,730 --> 00:22:32,970
Ertuğrul Ghazi and his sons' friendship
is eternal...

215
00:22:33,030 --> 00:22:34,920
and their hostility is the enemy's end.

216
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:40,540
Protect the Governor.

217
00:22:42,250 --> 00:22:44,630
Alps (men) get in the position!

218
00:22:44,850 --> 00:22:46,200
Protect the Governor.

219
00:22:51,250 --> 00:22:52,980
Alps(men), get in the position.

220
00:23:11,890 --> 00:23:14,140
This is treason!

221
00:23:14,260 --> 00:23:16,610
This is your castle, and those are your
soldiers.

222
00:23:16,610 --> 00:23:18,610
How could you let this treason happen?

223
00:23:23,030 --> 00:23:24,790
Whose dog are you?

224
00:23:24,840 --> 00:23:28,400
Who are you?
Speak up!

225
00:23:40,410 --> 00:23:41,500
Stop him!

226
00:24:10,230 --> 00:24:11,810
End him!

227
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:29,510
Osman.

228
00:24:30,470 --> 00:24:33,390
This castle is in sedition also, brothers.

229
00:24:33,630 --> 00:24:35,990
- Is everyone okay?
- Thanks to you, Osman.

230
00:24:35,990 --> 00:24:37,270
Thank Allah.

231
00:24:37,710 --> 00:24:42,670
If we don't figure out who is behind this,
sleep is haram (forbidden) for us.

232
00:24:44,560 --> 00:24:49,840
They will pay for this sooner or later.

233
00:25:16,370 --> 00:25:21,820
In this hard to live land, in Bithynia,
do you know how did I survive...

234
00:25:22,150 --> 00:25:25,350
and stay strong, Nizamettin Efendi? (Mr.)

235
00:25:28,300 --> 00:25:30,450
By smelling everything.

236
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:36,060
Both good and evil have a smell.

237
00:25:38,300 --> 00:25:42,180
No matter what you are, evil or good...

238
00:25:44,670 --> 00:25:46,960
you have to have a smell.

239
00:25:58,060 --> 00:26:01,860
Now, tell me.
What is the situation?

240
00:26:03,510 --> 00:26:06,170
Kayıs have gone to the castle, Alişer Bey.

241
00:26:06,430 --> 00:26:08,710
They will make an agreement with
the Governor.

242
00:26:09,320 --> 00:26:11,720
Do you think Governor will accept it?

243
00:26:11,780 --> 00:26:16,470
They are going with gifts.
Greeks are preparing a celebration.

244
00:26:22,710 --> 00:26:27,860
I am the letter, I am the pen, I am
the agreement in this land.

245
00:26:29,570 --> 00:26:33,140
Without me, that agreement is worthless.

246
00:26:33,690 --> 00:26:36,200
This will break the Yenipazar (the bazaar)

247
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:40,290
If they make an agreement, Söğütpazarı
(another bazaar) will rise in value.

248
00:26:50,620 --> 00:26:53,010
Obviously, this is going to be critical.

249
00:26:57,180 --> 00:26:59,010
But they miss something.

250
00:27:00,630 --> 00:27:05,100
The side that I am in always win.

251
00:27:25,730 --> 00:27:27,570
Zöhre Hatun.

252
00:27:28,700 --> 00:27:32,470
This incident has hurt me.

253
00:27:33,760 --> 00:27:37,680
I am so sorry.

254
00:27:37,860 --> 00:27:43,550
You can't get away with it by saying
sorry, princess.

255
00:27:52,190 --> 00:27:55,230
It was really devastating.

256
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:58,900
It was an inappropriate situation for
the great Kuluca Castle.

257
00:28:00,550 --> 00:28:04,970
Your castle is very elegant,
but obviously, its doors are weak.

258
00:28:06,230 --> 00:28:08,980
This disaster wouldn't have happened...

259
00:28:09,890 --> 00:28:12,670
if someone from inside hadn't helped.

260
00:28:16,790 --> 00:28:22,560
Yorgopolos will find the traitors
as fast as possible.

261
00:28:27,230 --> 00:28:30,270
Thanks to your braveness and militancy...

262
00:28:30,270 --> 00:28:32,720
my beloved husband is still alive.

263
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:39,500
He always praised Kayıs.

264
00:28:40,400 --> 00:28:43,250
Everyone would do the same.

265
00:28:43,630 --> 00:28:45,900
Peace and friendship needs this.

266
00:28:47,400 --> 00:28:49,370
This is why we are here, right?

267
00:28:50,370 --> 00:28:53,910
There are obstacles in peace and
friendship.

268
00:28:56,510 --> 00:28:59,490
The incident showed this to us.

269
00:29:00,780 --> 00:29:05,210
Apart from the Governor,
this attack was against my man also.

270
00:29:05,580 --> 00:29:09,960
As you said, I hope traitors will be found
as fast as possible, in sha Allah.

271
00:29:10,070 --> 00:29:14,780
Otherwise, neither Dündar Bey nor I will
drop this subject for sure (Evelallah)!

272
00:29:17,080 --> 00:29:20,330
- Excuse my apologize, Dündar Bey.
- Why would I?

273
00:29:20,450 --> 00:29:23,270
Me, Governor Yorgopolos...

274
00:29:23,360 --> 00:29:26,150
You need to find whoever did this...

275
00:29:26,590 --> 00:29:30,790
for me to accept your apology.

276
00:29:31,540 --> 00:29:34,380
Be sure that I'll find whoever did this.

277
00:29:34,890 --> 00:29:38,640
It is obvious that we annoyed someone
by signing this agreement, Dündar Bey.

278
00:29:38,650 --> 00:29:40,470
We almost died.

279
00:29:40,580 --> 00:29:44,880
Why would we trust you that you
keep your word?

280
00:29:45,100 --> 00:29:49,550
Furthermore, what about the conditions
that you have been postponing?

281
00:29:52,750 --> 00:29:55,820
If it will make you trust me again...

282
00:29:56,520 --> 00:30:00,330
- I am ready to accept them Dündar Bey.
- Governor Yorgopolos.

283
00:30:08,770 --> 00:30:10,370
Are you sure?

284
00:30:11,170 --> 00:30:15,840
Is making such an
important decision right?

285
00:30:15,860 --> 00:30:17,590
This is right, Kalonoz.

286
00:30:17,610 --> 00:30:19,410
Let's finish this today.

287
00:30:19,470 --> 00:30:24,050
So that Kayıs don't suspect
our friendship.

288
00:30:35,620 --> 00:30:37,660
What do you say, Gündüz Bey (master)?

289
00:30:38,020 --> 00:30:41,580
I say we finish this here today,
my Dündar Bey.

290
00:30:42,090 --> 00:30:46,480
When Ertuğrul Bey returns, we will
celebrate it in our tent.

291
00:30:47,320 --> 00:30:50,970
Let's finish this then.

292
00:30:51,370 --> 00:30:53,640
Let's sit.

293
00:31:11,320 --> 00:31:14,740
What about the indemnity of trade
caravans?

294
00:31:15,150 --> 00:31:17,470
These are so heavy conditions.

295
00:31:17,500 --> 00:31:21,500
This is valid for both sides, Commander
Kalanos.

296
00:31:21,780 --> 00:31:24,170
The one in whose lands crime happens...

297
00:31:24,680 --> 00:31:26,780
will pay it.

298
00:31:27,730 --> 00:31:32,370
After caravan raids, bandits have escaped.

299
00:31:32,910 --> 00:31:35,960
The indemnity would effect both of us.

300
00:31:36,610 --> 00:31:38,500
This is unaccaptable, Gündüz Bey.

301
00:31:39,170 --> 00:31:42,360
Of course, it is acceptable,
Commander Kalanos.

302
00:31:44,470 --> 00:31:45,510
Osman.

303
00:31:50,460 --> 00:31:52,640
How, Osman Bey?

304
00:31:54,540 --> 00:31:58,260
Bandits are reckless because they got
away with it.

305
00:32:00,180 --> 00:32:03,180
Every word coming out of your mouth is
precious for me.

306
00:32:03,700 --> 00:32:05,800
Continue your speech.

307
00:32:06,290 --> 00:32:10,760
If you authorize me to cross Hudut
and catch them...

308
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:14,700
bandits will realize they cannot escape.

309
00:32:15,370 --> 00:32:20,050
So, there will be no indemnity issue.

310
00:32:24,560 --> 00:32:27,470
Do you trust in yourself that much,
Osman Bey?

311
00:32:27,820 --> 00:32:30,620
He showed us his skillfulness today.

312
00:32:35,140 --> 00:32:37,340
What do you say, Dündar Bey?

313
00:32:38,080 --> 00:32:41,720
Your nephew Osman is right.

314
00:32:44,030 --> 00:32:46,200
My nephew thought it well.

315
00:32:46,800 --> 00:32:52,440
However, this way is both
hard and dangerous.

316
00:32:53,130 --> 00:32:58,280
Not everyone manage chasing bandits.

317
00:32:58,590 --> 00:33:03,890
If we give this mission to you, can you
manage it Osman Bey?

318
00:33:04,240 --> 00:33:08,830
This cannot be acceptable, this disregards
our borders, Governor Yorgopolos.

319
00:33:09,970 --> 00:33:13,340
If you give this mission to me and my
Alps...

320
00:33:14,660 --> 00:33:17,620
and a Commander that you assign...

321
00:33:17,620 --> 00:33:20,860
Kalanos would be relax too.

322
00:33:30,060 --> 00:33:36,850
Now that Dündar Bey also approves, I give
you the permission for my borders.

323
00:33:37,490 --> 00:33:40,920
I will arrange a Commander soon.

324
00:33:41,130 --> 00:33:45,560
You can think this as a mark of your
braveness.

325
00:33:45,580 --> 00:33:48,100
Thank you, Governor Yorgopolos.

326
00:33:48,280 --> 00:33:51,990
To the bandits who crossed the border...

327
00:34:06,230 --> 00:34:08,760
- Forgive, madam.
- Forgive madam.

328
00:34:18,320 --> 00:34:20,010
Forgive us madam.

329
00:34:24,270 --> 00:34:27,980
You couldn't even kill a old Governor.

330
00:34:29,370 --> 00:34:33,210
You ruined my plan which I worked on
so much...

331
00:34:33,310 --> 00:34:36,670
with your clumsiness.

332
00:35:12,880 --> 00:35:17,430
Osman could have known you Migala.

333
00:35:19,790 --> 00:35:24,560
Then, we couldn't explain anything.

334
00:35:25,160 --> 00:35:29,890
Now, take your best man.

335
00:35:30,480 --> 00:35:33,660
He must be killed in the first place.

336
00:35:36,690 --> 00:35:38,930
Don't underestimate Osman.

337
00:35:39,200 --> 00:35:41,150
He's not a random people.

338
00:35:42,990 --> 00:35:47,650
He must definitely pay this.

339
00:36:06,760 --> 00:36:08,290
Osman.

340
00:36:09,570 --> 00:36:11,460
Osman, what do you think you're doing?

341
00:36:11,760 --> 00:36:13,010
What, brother?

342
00:36:13,270 --> 00:36:17,910
Osman, weapons are held by soldiers,
words are said by elders.

343
00:36:18,180 --> 00:36:20,240
Why do you step in when
there's your uncle?

344
00:36:20,370 --> 00:36:22,950
The true word is said in point.

345
00:36:23,600 --> 00:36:28,170
La Hawla! Both you're looking for trouble
and you don't know your place?

346
00:36:28,750 --> 00:36:31,110
And you're still talking!

347
00:36:31,270 --> 00:36:32,980
No need to belabor.

348
00:36:33,800 --> 00:36:35,440
Enjoy your meal.

349
00:36:37,870 --> 00:36:40,020
Bora, stay here.

350
00:36:40,160 --> 00:36:42,270
Aybars, come with me.

351
00:37:02,860 --> 00:37:05,470
You'll look wonderful in your
henna night, Burçin.

352
00:37:14,510 --> 00:37:18,510
-My Aybars will like me a lot.
-He'll like you no matter what.

353
00:37:21,710 --> 00:37:24,790
One day, we'll hold a wedding for
you and Osman, Aygül.

354
00:37:26,180 --> 00:37:28,580
-You think so?
-Of course.

355
00:37:28,610 --> 00:37:32,610
When this time comes, I'll carry flour with
griddle and water with sieve for you.

356
00:37:34,540 --> 00:37:37,810
Inshaallah, Allah grants us a happiness
like yours.

357
00:37:37,940 --> 00:37:40,070
Insha'allah.

358
00:37:57,570 --> 00:38:00,010
They'll ruin everything!

359
00:38:07,210 --> 00:38:09,940
The only thing they care about is gold!

360
00:38:12,230 --> 00:38:14,500
My uncle and my brother don't get it.

361
00:38:14,540 --> 00:38:17,080
They don't see the sedition
in front of them.

362
00:38:17,160 --> 00:38:19,600
Who dares that, Osman Bey?

363
00:38:21,710 --> 00:38:24,550
It doesn't matter who dares, Aybars.

364
00:38:25,500 --> 00:38:28,970
Fortune of Kayıs is kneaded in
the chela of scorpion.

365
00:38:29,040 --> 00:38:31,040
We've always been under threat.

366
00:38:31,050 --> 00:38:33,820
And we're on alert.

367
00:38:35,460 --> 00:38:38,540
A great war will break out in this lands.

368
00:38:39,020 --> 00:38:41,650
I feel it in my bones.

369
00:38:43,090 --> 00:38:44,610
Never forget...

370
00:38:44,700 --> 00:38:48,700
This war will be won by warriors
like eagle and hawk...

371
00:38:49,330 --> 00:38:53,330
not by the ones who are
on alert like a pigeon.

372
00:38:56,530 --> 00:38:59,620
A state will rise from our dreams.

373
00:39:00,530 --> 00:39:03,140
A state...

374
00:39:05,020 --> 00:39:06,370
You heard Dündar Beys.

375
00:39:06,390 --> 00:39:10,830
You are talking about a state in the
middle of the turmoil, Osman Bey.

376
00:39:11,290 --> 00:39:13,340
We won't sleep anymore, Aybars.

377
00:39:13,970 --> 00:39:16,390
Things started to happen.

378
00:39:16,420 --> 00:39:19,930
It's time to hunt.

379
00:39:47,850 --> 00:39:49,840
Who are they, Osman Bey?

380
00:39:51,030 --> 00:39:54,540
Evil isn't only in the castle, my Aybars.

381
00:39:54,760 --> 00:39:57,160
Evil isn't only in the castle.

382
00:40:10,830 --> 00:40:12,540
Ya Allah!

383
00:40:28,200 --> 00:40:30,260
It's a trap, Aybars!

384
00:40:30,530 --> 00:40:33,710
You take the left, I'll take the
right. Eternal Allah!

385
00:40:33,750 --> 00:40:36,150
Allah is righteous!

386
00:40:59,590 --> 00:41:00,890
Aybars!

387
00:42:11,490 --> 00:42:12,880
Aybars!

388
00:42:26,030 --> 00:42:27,560
Aybars!

389
00:43:27,370 --> 00:43:28,630
Oh my Allah! Are you okay?

390
00:43:29,290 --> 00:43:31,110
I'm fine, I'm fine.

391
00:43:44,430 --> 00:43:47,930
Dropping blood stain on henna dress
brings bad luck, they say.

392
00:43:50,500 --> 00:43:52,710
It's because of excitement, my Burçin.

393
00:43:53,340 --> 00:43:55,240
You should interpret favourably.

394
00:43:55,310 --> 00:43:59,310
Think good, then it'll be good. Today
is your henna day.

395
00:44:09,920 --> 00:44:12,340
Aygül, they're not still back.

396
00:44:12,800 --> 00:44:14,580
Why are you worrying about them?

397
00:44:14,710 --> 00:44:17,340
First, we'll fit you nicely.

398
00:44:20,880 --> 00:44:24,200
Then when he sees you, he'll be shocked.

399
00:44:29,470 --> 00:44:32,170
My Allah, protect my Aybars.

400
00:45:10,990 --> 00:45:12,420
Catch that Turk!

401
00:45:13,170 --> 00:45:14,720
Come here, you smartasses.

402
00:45:55,900 --> 00:45:57,910
Run this way!

403
00:45:57,910 --> 00:49:03,510
www.kurulusosman.online

404
00:49:03,600 --> 00:49:06,300
If I oppose Osman's offer in
front of Tekfur...

405
00:49:06,360 --> 00:49:09,340
he'll think that we have hostility
between me and Osman.

406
00:49:09,480 --> 00:49:12,800
Osman does whatever he wants!

407
00:49:12,860 --> 00:49:15,820
If Osman storms around, you should rage.

408
00:49:15,860 --> 00:49:20,450
Or his idle moves will bring
our tent harm.

409
00:49:23,510 --> 00:49:25,060
Can I come in, uncle?

410
00:49:25,810 --> 00:49:27,500
Come, Gündüz.

411
00:49:35,080 --> 00:49:36,040
Uncle...

412
00:49:36,560 --> 00:49:38,620
No news from Osman and Aybars.

413
00:49:39,120 --> 00:49:41,160
They're not back.

414
00:49:44,090 --> 00:49:46,210
Don't think of troubling things, Gündüz.

415
00:49:48,160 --> 00:49:49,620
Uncle...

416
00:49:50,180 --> 00:49:52,120
I don't feel comfortable.

417
00:49:52,540 --> 00:49:55,040
Does Bamsı Bey know, Gündüz?

418
00:49:55,510 --> 00:49:56,640
No, uncle.

419
00:49:56,700 --> 00:49:58,680
Tell Alps to hit the road quickly.

420
00:49:58,700 --> 00:50:02,030
Tell them to go and don't return
without finding them.

421
00:50:03,030 --> 00:50:05,410
Your command, uncle.

422
00:50:41,020 --> 00:50:42,640
He may need help.

423
00:50:43,270 --> 00:50:44,930
We don't have much time.

424
00:51:30,950 --> 00:51:32,400
He's alive.

425
00:51:41,180 --> 00:51:42,960
We have to get him.

426
00:51:43,240 --> 00:51:45,160
We have to raise him from the dunghill.

427
00:52:13,010 --> 00:52:14,170
Pull...

428
00:52:14,450 --> 00:52:16,740
Come on, boy. Pull!

429
00:52:20,020 --> 00:52:21,290
Come on!

430
00:52:21,490 --> 00:52:23,720
Come on, boy!

431
00:52:25,350 --> 00:52:27,040
Come on!

432
00:52:28,010 --> 00:52:30,940
Come on! Come on, boy!

433
00:52:31,980 --> 00:52:34,550
Come on, boy!

434
00:53:17,330 --> 00:53:20,360
We lost so much time.

435
00:53:36,330 --> 00:53:38,780
He's pulling around.

436
00:54:06,360 --> 00:54:08,380
Help me. We have
to carry him.

437
00:54:50,930 --> 00:54:53,480
We have to go
now. Come on.

438
00:57:11,160 --> 00:57:12,650
Aybars!

439
00:57:21,960 --> 00:57:23,160
Aybars!

440
00:57:36,240 --> 00:57:37,890
Aybars!

441
00:57:44,750 --> 00:57:46,300
Aybars...

442
00:57:52,560 --> 00:57:54,160
Aybars...

443
00:57:58,410 --> 00:58:00,160
Aybars!

444
00:58:13,310 --> 00:58:14,900
Aybars!

445
00:58:18,060 --> 00:58:19,860
Aybars!

446
00:58:26,230 --> 00:58:29,060
Mashaallah! Come here, come.

447
00:58:30,860 --> 00:58:32,590
Come.

448
00:58:33,120 --> 00:58:35,640
Come here. Come...

449
00:58:35,660 --> 00:58:39,150
I don't want to hurt you. I don't
want to hurt you at all.

450
00:58:39,180 --> 00:58:43,180
But I wish to sacrifice you for Allah...

451
00:58:43,220 --> 00:58:47,770
and offer you to Alps in my
Aybars' wedding.

452
00:58:59,640 --> 00:59:01,440
Mashaallah!

453
00:59:02,300 --> 00:59:04,620
Im grateful to you.

454
00:59:04,730 --> 00:59:08,730
What would we do if...

455
00:59:08,880 --> 00:59:11,210
Allah hadn't given you to us?

456
00:59:11,840 --> 00:59:15,840
But would it be easy cutting my own son...

457
00:59:19,060 --> 00:59:21,390
with our own knife...

458
00:59:22,070 --> 00:59:24,400
to sacrifice him to Allah?

459
00:59:25,090 --> 00:59:26,870
Would it be?

460
00:59:29,560 --> 00:59:33,210
It wouldn't be. It wouldn't.

461
00:59:33,340 --> 00:59:37,340
Do you know that story? Will you listen
to me if I tell you?

462
00:59:37,820 --> 00:59:41,170
Listen to me, then.

463
00:59:47,760 --> 00:59:49,160
Aybars!

464
01:00:00,600 --> 01:00:02,230
Brother...

465
01:00:02,860 --> 01:00:04,580
My brother...

466
01:00:04,630 --> 01:00:06,710
My dear brother...

467
01:00:15,130 --> 01:00:17,580
Thank Allah, before my death...

468
01:00:18,310 --> 01:00:20,440
I saw you safe and sound.

469
01:00:20,500 --> 01:00:23,690
People's fate save them from
their death, brother. Hang on!

470
01:00:23,750 --> 01:00:26,670
Hang on! I'll carry you. Come on!

471
01:00:27,860 --> 01:00:29,500
Hang on, brother.

472
01:00:35,100 --> 01:00:37,190
Hang on, my Aybars.

473
01:00:37,910 --> 01:00:39,360
Hang on, brother.

474
01:00:42,300 --> 01:00:46,300
Prophet Abraham's only wish...

475
01:00:46,430 --> 01:00:48,930
was to have children.

476
01:00:50,100 --> 01:00:54,150
He wanted from Allah and he said...

477
01:00:54,560 --> 01:00:59,690
"If you give me a child, I'll
sacrifice him for you."

478
01:01:00,570 --> 01:01:05,730
And Allah gave him a child
from our Mother Hacer.

479
01:01:06,610 --> 01:01:11,600
Prophet Abraham named his child "İsmail."

480
01:01:12,660 --> 01:01:14,550
İsmail grew up.

481
01:01:14,690 --> 01:01:17,170
He was 7.

482
01:01:41,350 --> 01:01:43,370
You look beautiful.

483
01:01:43,580 --> 01:01:45,270
Great!

484
01:01:45,360 --> 01:01:47,010
Smile a little bit.

485
01:01:47,380 --> 01:01:50,900
A bride shouldn't sulk before her henna.

486
01:01:51,470 --> 01:01:54,140
I'll complain about you when Aybars comes.

487
01:01:54,160 --> 01:01:57,160
I'll tell him that my dear sister sulked
me when you're away.

488
01:01:57,210 --> 01:02:00,720
I'm sorry, my Aygül. I upset you.

489
01:02:01,000 --> 01:02:03,380
No, you don't.

490
01:02:04,200 --> 01:02:07,630
Then Prophet Abraham saw a dream.

491
01:02:07,820 --> 01:02:11,820
In his dream, he was said about
him sacrificing his child.

492
01:02:13,350 --> 01:02:17,050
And Abraham went nearby İsmail...

493
01:02:17,590 --> 01:02:21,590
and told him about his dream.

494
01:02:23,620 --> 01:02:27,620
İsmail looked at his father's eyes...

495
01:02:28,060 --> 01:02:29,890
He said "father"...

496
01:02:29,930 --> 01:02:33,300
"Do what's necessary!"

497
01:02:40,080 --> 01:02:44,920
İbrahim's heart was broken...

498
01:02:46,110 --> 01:02:50,110
but the order was...

499
01:02:50,480 --> 01:02:52,500
a holy order.

500
01:02:56,390 --> 01:02:59,810
And he... he...

501
01:03:00,370 --> 01:03:02,060
took İsmail and...

502
01:03:02,210 --> 01:03:04,580
laid him down to his forehead.

503
01:03:05,650 --> 01:03:10,060
He was about to stab him....

504
01:03:19,360 --> 01:03:21,260
May it be hayır. (something good.)

505
01:03:25,130 --> 01:03:26,930
I hope there's nothin wrong.

506
01:03:55,400 --> 01:03:56,930
Is he Osman?

507
01:04:05,770 --> 01:04:07,390
We're here.

508
01:04:12,370 --> 01:04:14,690
Inform the healer quickly.

509
01:04:14,840 --> 01:04:16,290
Come on!

510
01:04:18,690 --> 01:04:20,570
Come on!

511
01:04:20,870 --> 01:04:22,710
Summon the healer!

512
01:04:22,830 --> 01:04:24,880
Hang on, my Aybars!

513
01:04:53,080 --> 01:04:54,650
Aybars...

514
